  "summary": "When Tim Costello was in 9th grade, he asked his teacher if poverty was something that just naturally happens—like the tide or sunrise. He learned it wasn't natural, but caused by human decisions and policies. Now 69, he's spent more than 30 years fighting poverty in Australia and around the world. He's visited places hit by wars and disasters, was once mayor of St Kilda, wrote books, and is considered a national treasure. People sometimes mix him up with his brother, Peter Costello, who was Australia's treasurer and is linked to the Liberal Party. Tim is well-known as a Baptist minister and led the charity World Vision for 13 years."
